ECOSYSTEM ATTRIBUTION
=====================

Inkan builds on patterns published by the Midnight Foundation and the wider
ecosystem. Where a file adapts someone else's code closely, its header says so.
This file records the debts that are architectural.

Every Compact circuit and every witness implementation is original to this
project. What was borrowed is design, and it is listed so a reader can go and
check the originals.

Midnight Foundation (https://github.com/midnightntwrk)
------------------------------------------------------

  midnightntwrk/midnight-local-dev                      Apache-2.0
  midnightntwrk/example-bboard                          Apache-2.0
      `contracts/midnight/inkan/scripts/lib/wallet.ts` adapts the wallet
      construction, sync, funding and DUST-registration sequence from these two.
      The surrounding structure, the retry on a registration fee that has not yet
      accrued, and the block-limit probe are ours.

  midnightntwrk/example-zkloan                          Apache-2.0
      The identity model. Every party key is a domain-separated hash of a
      witness-held secret, and `ownPublicKey()` is never used to authorise
      anything, as the Midnight security guidance requires.

OpenZeppelin (https://github.com/OpenZeppelin/compact-contracts)
----------------------------------------------------------------

  ForwarderShielded                                      MIT
      The shape of `payInvoiceShielded`: the contract receives the buyer's
      shielded coin and forwards it to the seller in the same call, so it never
      holds the money. Read for the pattern; no code was copied.
